{title: While Shepherds Watched Their Flocks}
{artist: Nahum Tate / George F. Handel}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955) # 169)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]While shepherds [A]watched [G]their [D]flocks by night,
[D]All seated on the [A7]ground,
[A7]The an[D]gel [Em]of [A7]the [D]Lord came down,
[D]And glory shone around,
[D]And glory shone around.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Fear not! said [A]he, [G]for [D]mighty dread
[D]Had seized their troubled [A7]mind.
[A7]“Glad tid[D]ings [Em]of [A7]great [D]joy I bring
[D]To you and all mankind
[D]To you and all mankind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]“To you, in [A]Da[G]vid’s [D]town, this day
[D]Is born of David’s [A7]line
[A7]A Sav[D]ior, [Em]who [A7]is [D]Christ the Lord,
[D]And this shall be the sign,
[D]And this shall be the sign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]The heav’nly [A]Babe [G]you [D]there shall find
[D]To human view dis[A7]played,
[A7]All mean[D]ly [Em]wrapped [A7]in [D]swathing bands,
[D]And in a manger laid,
[D]And in a manger laid.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Thus spake the [A]ser[G]aph [D]and forthwith
[D]Appeared a shining [A7]throng
[A7]Of an[D]gels [Em]prais[A7]ing [D]God on high,
[D]Who thus addressed their song,
[D]Who thus addressed their song:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]All glory [A]be [G]to [D]God on high,
[D]And to the Earth be [A7]peace;
[A7]Good will [D]hence[Em]forth [A7]from [D]Heav’n to men
[D]Begin and never cease,
[D]Begin and never cease!
{end_of_verse}
